{title: And Can It Be}
{artist: Charles Wesley}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[G]And can it be that [C]I should [G]gain an [Am]interest [D]in the [G]Savior's blood?
[G]Died he for me, who [C]caused his [G]pain? For [Am]me, who [D]him to [G]death pursued?
A[D]mazing love! How [G]can it be that [C]thou, my [G]God, shouldst [D]die for [G]me?

Chorus
A[D]mazing love! How [G]can it [C]be
that [G]thou, my [D]God, shouldst [G]die for me?

Verse 2
[G]'Tis mystery all: th'Immortal [C]dies: Who [G]can explore [Am]His [D]strange [G]design? In
[G]vain the firstborn seraph [C]tries To [G]sound [Am]the depths [D]of [G]love divine.
'Tis mercy all! [G]Let earth adore, [C]Let angel [G]minds [D]inquire no [G]more.

Verse 3
[G]He left His Father's throne [C]above [G]So free, [Am]so [D]infinite His [G]grace? Emptied
[G]Himself of all but [C]love, And [G]bled for [Am]Adam's helpless [D]race: [G]'Tis mercy
all, immense and [G]free, For O [C]my God, [G]it [D]found out [G]me!

Verse 4
[G]Long my imprisoned spirit lay, [C]Fast [G]bound in [Am]sin [D]and nature's [G]night; Thine
[G]eye diffused a quick'ning ray? [C]I woke, [G]the [Am]dungeon flamed [D]with light; [G]My chains
fell off, my [G]heart was free, [C]I rose, [G]went forth, [D]and followed [G]Thee.

Verse 5
[G]Still the small inward voice [C]I [G]hear, That [Am]whispers [D]all my [G]sins forgiv'n;
[G]Still the atoning blood is [C]near, That [G]quenched [Am]the wrath [D]of hostile [G]Heav'n. I
feel the life [G]His wounds impart; [C]I feel [G]the Savior [D]in my [G]heart.
